  "id": "doppler-effect",
  "term": "Doppler effect",
  "definition": "The Doppler effect is a change in the frequency observed for a sound because of movement between the sound source and the listener or recording point. In this context, it is considered as a possible reason why whale calls might be measured at different frequencies at different times.",
